

COLOR(1)            UNIX Programmer's Manual               COLOR(1)



NAME
     color - set console foreground, background, or border color

SYNOPSIS
     color -fg|-bg|-bd name
     color -fg|-bg -x RRGGBB

DESCRIPTION
     _C_o_l_o_r rewrites the console's default palette slots (fore-
     ground/background) or the IIgs border color.  The 16 ANSI
     color names are: black red green yellow blue magenta cyan
     white gray brightred brightgreen brightyellow brightblue
     brightmagenta brightcyan brightwhite.

     -x takes six hex digits; each channel is truncated to its
     high nibble (the SHR palette is 4 bits per channel).  The
     border carries only the 16 hardware colors, so -bd does not
     accept -x.

SEE ALSO
     font(1)

